smb: client: get rid of @nlsc param in cifs_tree_connect()

jira KERNEL-814
Rebuild_History Non-Buildable kernel-4.18.0-553.115.1.el8_10
commit-author Paulo Alcantara <pc@manguebit.com>
commit b2fe4a8fa0f6b9dbb7d4965f71ec72191cda34f1
Empty-Commit: Cherry-Pick Conflicts during history rebuild.
Will be included in final tarball splat. Ref for failed cherry-pick at:
ciq/ciq_backports/kernel-4.18.0-553.115.1.el8_10/b2fe4a8f.failed

We can access local_nls directly from @tcon->ses, so there is no need
to pass it as parameter in cifs_tree_connect().

	Signed-off-by: Paulo Alcantara (Red Hat) <pc@manguebit.com>
	Signed-off-by: Steve French <stfrench@microsoft.com>
(cherry picked from commit b2fe4a8fa0f6b9dbb7d4965f71ec72191cda34f1)
	Signed-off-by: Jonathan Maple <jmaple@ciq.com>

